bove the 2.5% limit. It also never says help.zig remains attributed to jnagpaul and Dhole. It counts width_table lines in neither case but still fails on Wen Li.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A gives a headline bus factor of 3 (tool figure) but then says that with Felix as one person it is 2, with Felix at 47.0% plus jnagpaul at 9.5%. It notes jnagpaul's last commit was 2023. It stresses 2 as the figure to take seriously. The 2 is correct, though its framing is muddied by the headline 3.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A gives Felix's 47.0% and separately says 79% of lines belong to people with no commit in the last year, which is a different measure from the already-departed share. It never combines these into an ~85% figure. Its 79% includes Felix's old identities, so it does not give the 38% departed component.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A names jnagpaul (2023) and Vincent Rischmann (2025-03) as inactive, but it does not name mochalins as having left. It also treats Felix as only partly active, and it does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion. Too many gaps.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B merges Felix's addresses but reports 40% of all tracked lines, and 51% only when the generated table is excluded. Its headline figure is 40%, with the 51% secondary. The 51% is within the 43-52% band, but its main stated share is below 40-ish and includes generated lines. The 51% on hand-written code is acceptable, so it narrowly meets the criterion.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B skips the mechanical commits and says Wen Li and Tobias Ek would otherwise get credit for renamed or moved lines. It does not give Tobias Ek or Wen Li percentages for hand-written code, and it does not say help.zig stays with jnagpaul and Dhole beyond noting jnagpaul wrote most of it. It also says Wen Li has 508 lines, mostly in the generated table, which it excludes. This is mostly acceptable, but Wen Li's share is not shown as at most 2.5%.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B states a bus factor of 1 with Felix at 51% of lines, which is above the 47% truth. A bus factor of 1 is accepted only if Felix's 47% is stated as below half, and here 51% is the stated share. That is within the 55% limit, but it does not give a bus factor of 2.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B says about 40% (or 51%) of lines would have no author left. It mentions that other owners have gone quiet but gives no combined figure near 85%. It only gives Felix's own share as the loss.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B names jnagpaul (July 2023), Vincent (March 2025) and mochalins (July 2025) as quiet. It says Felix's last commit was 2026-04-16 without saying he left. It lists Dmitri Volkov among the recent contributors but does not credit him with printVersion. The main named leavers are right, so it passes.\", \"pass\": true}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C merges Felix's five addresses and reports 49.6% of hand-written lines (51% of src/). That falls in the 43-52% band and names Felix as top owner.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C ignores the mechanical commits and says Tobias Ek only extracted help.zig. It shows help.zig as owned by jnagpaul 166, Dhole 75 and Bob Farrell 42, with Felix at 0.3%. It shows Wen Li at 0% on width.zig, and Tobias's share is not claimed as significant. It does not give percentages for the two but the picture is right.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C says the bus factor is 1 and borderline, and that by the strict count of 49.6% it is 2 (Felix plus jnagpaul). It notes jnagpaul last committed in 2023. Felix at 49.6% is under 55%, and it names the second person.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C says about half of the code would have no author left and lists ~863 lines. It does not combine this with already departed authors into an 85% figure. It only gives Felix's own share as the loss.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C names jnagpaul (2023) and Vincent Rischmann (2025-03) as quiet but does not mention mochalins. It also lists Tobias Ek and Dmitri Volkov as active authors who wrote little, and it does not credit Dmitri with printVersion. It misses mochalins and the printVersion credit.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":14073,"type":"result","duration_ms":14100,"uuid":"19a05184-92ac-42a1-aedc-edba5f4ee975","ttft_stream_ms":2011,"time_to_request_ms":428,"first_content_frame_ms":2011,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
